/T (Abstract  This report details the process of network traffic inspection using Wireshark, centered on analyzing a standard HTTP web browsing session. By capturing packets generated during a website request, the report provides a detailed breakdown of the dependency on DNS resolution, the TCP/IP connection establishment \(three-way handshake\), the subsequent HTTP GET request and 200 OK response, and the connection termination. The analysis confirms the layered structure of network communication and highlights Wireshark's capability to provide essential insights into network performance, resource utilization, and potential security vulnerabilities. )
/E (Abstract  This report details the process of network traffic inspection using Wireshark, centered on analyzing a standard HTTP web browsing session. By capturing packets generated during a website request, the report provides a detailed breakdown of the dependency on DNS resolution, the TCP/IP connection establishment \(three-way handshake\), the subsequent HTTP GET request and 200 OK response, and the connection termination. The analysis confirms the layered structure of network communication and highlights Wireshark's capability to provide essential insights into network performance, resource utilization, and potential security vulnerabilities. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
