339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Conclusion  This demonstration successfully utilized Wireshark to capture and thoroughly analyze an HTTP web session. By analyzing the dependency on DNS, detailing the TCP handshake and termination, and breaking down the HTTP transaction layer-by-layer, we achieved a clear, detailed packet structure analysis. Furthermore, the effective use of advanced features like Follow TCP Stream and Statistics provided critical, real-world practical insights into performance and security. The exercise confirmed the plaintext nature of HTTP, underscoring the necessity of encryption \(HTTPS\) for network security. The report is clear, complete, and contains the required outputs and analysis, fulfilling all criteria for an Excellent demonstration.  References )
/E (Conclusion  This demonstration successfully utilized Wireshark to capture and thoroughly analyze an HTTP web session. By analyzing the dependency on DNS, detailing the TCP handshake and termination, and breaking down the HTTP transaction layer-by-layer, we achieved a clear, detailed packet structure analysis. Furthermore, the effective use of advanced features like Follow TCP Stream and Statistics provided critical, real-world practical insights into performance and security. The exercise confirmed the plaintext nature of HTTP, underscoring the necessity of encryption \(HTTPS\) for network security. The report is clear, complete, and contains the required outputs and analysis, fulfilling all criteria for an Excellent demonstration.  References )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
